# Sanity CMS

Marketing content lives in Sanity. Assessments, users, and dashboard data stay in Neon.

## Layout

| Piece | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Standalone Studio | `studio-productive-leadership/` (port 3333) |
| Embedded Studio | `/studio` (`app/src/app/studio/`) |
| Config | `app/sanity.config.js`, `app/src/sanity/env.js`, `studio-productive-leadership/sanity.config.js` |
| Schemas | `app/src/sanity/schemaTypes/` (keep in sync with `studio-productive-leadership/schemaTypes/`) |
| Client / GROQ | `app/src/sanity/lib/client.js`, `app/src/sanity/lib/queries.js` |
| Page builder UI | `app/src/slices/` rendered by `SliceZone` |

## Fetching

Use `sanityFetch()` from `app/src/sanity/lib/client.js`. Tag requests with `sanity` so `/api/revalidate` can purge them. If `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID` is missing, fetches return `null` and the site uses static fallbacks.

Do not query Sanity from Client Components. Keep reads in Server Components and the existing adapters (`getSiteSettings`, `getHeaderMenuLinks`, `getFooterMenuLinks`, `buildPageMetadata`).

## Modeling

- Singletons (`homepage`, `settings`, `headerMenu`, `footerMenu`, `articleListing`) use fixed document IDs
- Repeatable pages use `slug`; articles live at `/articles/[slug]`
- Page builder slices are objects in a `slices` array (`hero`, `about`, `media`, `textImage`, `listing`, `sectionIntro`, `richText`, `cookiebotCookieListing`)
- Links are `appLink` (path/URL + optional page or article reference)
- Rich text is Portable Text (`portableText`), rendered only through the `RichText` molecule
- Articles may be **protected**; unsigned visitors see a padlock in the listing and cannot read the body

## Avoid

- `@prismicio/*` or Slice Machine
- Fetching Sanity from the browser for published page content
- Rendering Portable Text without the shared `RichText` components
